WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.650
In 1930, a man in homespun cloth
set out on foot for the sea.

2
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.970
He walked about 390 kilometres.

3
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.900
His goal was to make a pinch of salt.

4
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.620
Making salt broke a British tax.

5
00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.510
It was a political act.

6
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.920
Yet the same man fasted,
read the Bhagavad Gita,

7
00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.840
and said his politics
came from his religion.

8
00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:27.100
So was Gandhi a saint, a
politician, or something else?

9
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.910
In this mission, you'll unpack satyagraha,

10
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.940
his name for truth-force, and
where he believed it came from.

11
00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:38.890
Then you'll see who claims Gandhi today,
from Indian Hindus and Dalit thinkers

12
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.550
to the wider world.

13
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.650
Your mission: weigh up
whether Gandhi was a saint,

14
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.030
a politician, or both at once.
